                                Wiltshire, Benedictine Abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St
                                Aldhelm</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following context for the rejection:
                                See Edwin Wolf II, <title>Descriptive Catalogue of the John
                                    Frederick Lewis Collection of European Manuscripts</title>
                                (Philadelphia, 1937), no. 84: <q>Arms of abbey of Malmesbury in the
                                illuminated border, fol. 32v, repeated 8 times (gules 2 leopards
                                argent a chief argent overall an episcopal crozier in pale).</q> These,
                                however, are not the arms of Malmesbury, which has in chief a mitre
                                between two croziers.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">George E.
                                Leighton</persName> of St Louis, sold New York 25 April 1929, n. 83
                            (facsimile). No. 276 in a French bookseller's catalogue.</provenance>
